Actual source23 1d3ed25bea2c8b781f7ee5a178af0f66061b3984 versus24 7db08eac6ead99d641834c56ccec06a06600586a is frozen. Both require77 exported files and the exact14 named CTests, nearest fifth/PV sixth, before hosted readiness. Actual native42/active8/PV56/TT12/SEE504 and56 parent cold/warm searches passed; first native24 signature292545 is now bound. Actual23 original candidate-side capture is reused under its original BOTH receipt/label; one new24 process supplies genuine ONE24 receipt/five rows. Complete original source/core/raw/native/root/independent receipts are bound.

The calibrated design remains excluded ABBA warmup,15 same-binary A/A blocks then31 counterbalanced A/B blocks,5bench11 commands per process,188processes/940commands. Exact-child wait4 CPU and whole-process monotonic wall use identical calibration gates and shared-index whole-block10000-draw bootstrap seed20261102; both95% lower bounds must exceed1 after normal completion/final byte-mode integrity. Failure stops acceptance without retry/rescue/pooling. Bounds remain690s build/3600s timing/60s sample,90/12/65minute workflow/job steps as declared. This measures startup+five complete engine benchmarks, not a pure SEE kernel or Elo.

Owned helper461a and archive952a remain unchanged. NEW24 alone carries the reviewed outer affinity-finally repair; hash/context/save and restoration failures are fatal when Python finally runs. Original21 code, initial42 tests/61seal/118disabled review and genuine adapter RED/GREEN/46test phase remain retained separately. Current code differs from approved postcapture consumer only by the genuine292545 scalar and literal finite-proof capture path; analysis changes only that scalar.

READY metadata permits no inference of a completed hosted run or gain. Root authorization remains launch_authorized_now=false until separate independent final enabled review, root fixed-payload rehash/publication/readback and sole authorized prefix push. Branch-only event excludes tags; per-run attempt1 is not a global one-use guard, and no fixed HEAD guard exists in workflow. Root must ensure the sole trigger uses the exact reviewed object. No Windows/Ryzen, Stockfish or Elo claim is made. All original normal/failure logs and raw evidence are preserved through separate always archive/upload/fresh-results steps when the host can execute them.
''')
 changes={str(P/'common.py'):Q/'common.py',str(P/'analysis.py'):Q/'analysis.py',str(P/'protocol.json'):Q/'protocol.json',str(P/'README.md'):Q/'README.md',str(R/common.WORKFLOW):Q/'forge-hosted-see-proof-performance.yml'}
 manifest=[]
 for p in sorted([p for p in P.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.name!='PACKAGE-SHA256SUMS']+[R/common.WORKFLOW]):
  replacement=changes.get(str(p),p);manifest.append(sha(replacement)+'  '+p.relative_to(R).as_posix()+'\n')
 (Q/'PACKAGE-SHA256SUMS').write_text(''.join(manifest));changes[str(P/'PACKAGE-SHA256SUMS')]=Q/'PACKAGE-SHA256SUMS'
 frozen=common.snapshot(list(consumed_proofs)+transport+common.inventory(R,P));assert common.rehash(frozen)['status']=='passed'
 code={p.relative_to(R).as_posix():sha(changes.get(str(p),p)) for p in sorted(P.glob('*.py'))}
 result={'status':'PASS_ACTUAL_READY_PROPOSAL_NOT_APPLIED_NOT_LAUNCHED','baseline_sha':BASE,'candidate_sha':CAND,'current_native_ctests_each':42,'current_active_tsan_each':8,'actual_source_files_each':77,'actual_proof_count':len(proofs),'transport_records':len(transport),'mandatory_omission_controls':controls,'metadata_negative_controls':negatives,'frozen_inputs':frozen,'frozen_input_count':len(frozen),'proposed_execution_code_sha256':code,'proposed_replacements':{n:{'proposal_path':str(p),'sha256':sha(p),'current_sha256':sha(Path(n)),'current_mode':stat.S_IMODE(Path(n).stat().st_mode)} for n,p in changes.items()},'proposed_workflow_sha256':cfg['workflow_sha256'],'root_preparation_sha256':sha(V/'ROOT-PREPARATION-REVIEW.json'),'root_authorization_sha256':sha(V/'ROOT-ONE-ATTEMPT-AUTHORIZATION.json'),'independent_finite_review_sha256':sha(V/'independent-review/REVIEW.json'),'oldphase61_118_42_and_current46_preserved':True,'tests_run_by_this_builder':False,'engines_builds_helpers_matches_git_network_triggers':0,'final_independent_enabled_review_required':True,'root_launch_authorized_now':False,'speed_or_elo_claim':None}
 return result

def main():
 p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--proof-map',type=Path,required=True);p.add_argument('--out',type=Path,required=True);a=p.parse_args();result=prepare(a.proof_map.resolve(strict=True))
 with a.out.open('x') as f:json.dump(result,f,indent=2);f.write('\n')
